  "prompt": "How did each segment's MRR change over 2025? MRR comes from subscription_events: a subscription's MRR on a date is the sum of its mrr_delta_local with event_date on or before that date, in its subscriptions.currency. Give each segment's MRR on 31 December 2024 and on 31 December 2025, and change_mrr, the 2025 figure minus the 2024 one. Convert both balances at the same fixed rate, that of 31 December 2025 (fx_rates.eur_per_unit for the subscription's currency on 2025-12-31), so the change shows no currency effect. Round all three to 2 decimals with ROUND. Return four columns, in this order: segment, mrr_2024, mrr_2025 and change_mrr. Return one row for each segment. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "segment",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "mrr_2024",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
